  "_doc": [
    "Exact number of GPU-aligned ordered-add sites (in-place `fadd vD.4s, vD.4s, vM.4s` from addOrderedNEON) per native NEON tile program, per compiler identity and ISA envelope.",
    "Keys: rows:family:policy:encoding:map:minimum as in CPUNativeTileRegisterBudget.json. Only GPU-aligned (policy 1) programs are named; backend-native programs must hold none.",
    "A site is counted in the executed compile's own assembler input (the GNU plan's cc*.s, replayed into the bound object) and bound to the identical object instruction at the same index.",
    "The witness requires equality in both directions: a change that turns one ordered addition back into a plain one, or adds one, fails until this file is changed in a reviewed diff.",
    "Integrated assemblers (AppleClang/Clang -cc1 -emit-obj) have no assembler input to retain, so no counts are committed for them and their proof fails closed."
  ]
